  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015) is set up for his contrast CT on Mon 10/26 at 9:00, with the RBC-RAD-07 prep in place.\n\n- **CT order (sr-t0001):** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast, for pancreatic cyst surveillance. It's linked to his booked appointment (appt-00001). The order catalog only had the general contrast CT, not a separate pancreatic-protocol code, so the order reason says GI asked for pancreatic protocol.\n- **Contrast allergy:** The radiology report from the day of his 2019 reaction calls it moderate: hives and mild eyelid swelling, no airway or breathing problems. The policy grades by that report. The \"anaphylaxis\" entry on his allergy list was added in 2021 from his own account, so it doesn't change the grade. That means he gets premedication rather than a no-contrast/radiologist consult. Shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies don't count as risk factors.\n- **Premedication:**\n  - Prednisone 50 mg at 8 PM Sunday 10/25, 2 AM Monday and 8 AM Monday (mr-t0002).\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg at 8 AM Monday (mr-t0003).\n  - He can't drive after the diphenhydramine and needs a driver.\n- **Kidney function:** He was in the ER 10/16–17 with dehydration and acute kidney injury. His creatinine was 1.94, then 1.46 at discharge, against a baseline of about 1.0. Those values don't count as a kidney check under the policy. I ordered a new creatinine to be drawn before 8:30 AM Monday (sr-t0004) for the radiologist to review that morning. The scan stays as booked.\n- **Metformin:** On hold now (mr-00189), through the scan and at least 48 hours after. I ordered a repeat creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006). I also set a task for you (task-t0007) to review it and restart metformin only if kidney function is back to normal. That repeat also covers the 1-week kidney follow-up the ER asked for.\n- **Patient message (comm-t0008):** He was told:\n  - to get the blood draw before the scan;\n  - the exact pill times, and that he needs a driver;\n  - to stop metformin and not restart until told;\n  - to drink fluids and tell CT staff about the 2019 reaction;\n  - when to call the clinic or 911.\n- **Note:** Everything is documented in a progress note (doc-t0009).\n\n**For you to decide:** I left the \"anaphylaxis\" allergy entry (alg-00009) as it is. It conflicts with the 2019 report, so you may want to correct it.",
  "resumed": false,
